{"issue": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2896", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2896/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2896/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2896/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/2896", "id": 4625830216, "node_id": "I_kwDOBabE0s8AAAABE7iRSA", "number": 2896, "title": "Android: camera definition fails to load, Camera.getCurrentSettings() returns UNAVAILABLE", "user": {"login": "rkganeri", "id": 64553818, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjY0NTUzODE4", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64553818?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/rkganeri", "html_url": "https://github.com/rkganeri", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/rkganeri/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/rkganeri/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/rkganeri/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/rkganeri/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/rkganeri/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/rkganeri/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/rkganeri/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/rkganeri/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/rkganeri/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [], "state": "closed", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 4, "created_at": "2026-06-09T21:40:14Z", "updated_at": "2026-08-11T13:24:09Z", "closed_at": "2026-08-11T13:24:09Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "## Description\nI'm using MAVSDK Java / Android with `mavsdk_server` on an Android controller. The vehicle has a MAVLink camera component that advertises a camera definition (`camera_definition-ILX-LR1_Sony-40847.xml`). The camera is discovered correctly, but the MAVSDK Camera plugin never seems to load the camera definition, and `Camera.getCurrentSettings(componentId)` returns `UNAVAILABLE`.\n\nThis prevents reading the current camera settings through the Camera plugin. Setting camera params through other paths can still affect the camera, but MAVSDK cannot read back the settings.\n\nAfter camera discovery, I can see the failure logs:\n```\nD/Mavsdk  : Component Camera 1 (100) added.\nE/Mavsdk  : Cannot open file \"/data/data/com.dronebase.af.app.px4\nD/Mavsdk  : Cache hit for camera_definition-ILX-LR1_Sony-40847.xml\nE/Mavsdk  : Failed to open \"/data/data/com.dronebase.af.app.px4\nI/Mavsdk  : Using cached file \"/data/data/com.dronebase.af.app.px4\nE/Mavsdk  : tinyxml2::LoadFile failed: Error=XML_ERROR_FILE_READ_ERROR ErrorID=5 (0x5) Line number=0\nE/Mavsdk  : Failed to load camera definition: \"/data/data/com.dronebase.af.app.px4\n...\nio.mavsdk.camera.Camera$CameraException: UNAVAILABLE: Unavailable\n\tat io.mavsdk.camera.Camera$19.onNext(Camera.java:2006)\n\tat io.mavsdk.camera.Camera$19.onNext(Camera.java:1999)\n\tat io.grpc.stub.ClientCalls$StreamObserverToCallListenerAdapter.onMessage(ClientCalls.java:468)\n\tat io.grpc.internal.ClientCallImpl$ClientStreamListenerImpl$1MessagesAvailable.runInternal(ClientCallImpl.java:667)\n\tat io.grpc.internal.ClientCallImpl$ClientStreamListenerImpl$1MessagesAvailable.runInContext(ClientCallImpl.java:654)\n\tat io.grpc.internal.ContextRunnable.run(ContextRunnable.java:37)\n\tat io.grpc.internal.SerializingExecutor.run(SerializingExecutor.java:133)\n\tat java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor.runWorker(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:1100)\n\tat java.util.concurrent.ThreadPoolExecutor$Worker.run(ThreadPoolExecutor.java:624)\n\tat java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:1572)\n```\n\n## Potential Source\nThis looks like it may be related to the `ANDROID` branch of the `get_cache_directory()` [function here](https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/blob/main/cpp/src/mavsdk/core/fs_utils.cpp#L70). That code reads `/proc/self/cmdline`. On Android this is NUL-separated, and in our app the first arg includes a trailing NUL:\n```\n/proc/self/cmdline first-arg=\"com.dronebase.af.app.px4?\" (hasEmbeddedNul=true)\n```\n\nThe resulting cache path appears to be truncated to `/data/data/com.dronebase.af.app.px4`. This is the package root but not the MavSDK cache directory `/data/data/com.dronebase.af.app.px4/mavsdk_cache`.  Because the process name still contains the NUL separator from `/proc/self/cmdline`, native file operations appear to truncate the path before `/mavsdk_cache`. \n\nThere is already a [comment](https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/blob/main/cpp/src/mavsdk/core/fs_utils.cpp#L75) indicating that the trailing `\\0` should be stripped, but the current check appears to dereference `line.end()`. Since `end()` is one past the last character, this does not reliably test the trailing byte. The package name can retain the NUL separator and produce a path that is later truncated by native file operations.", "closed_by": {"login": "JonasVautherin", "id": 2606672, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI2MDY2NzI=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2606672?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin", "html_url": "https://github.com/JonasVautherin", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/